---
import GuideLayout from "@/layouts/GuideLayout.astro";
---

<GuideLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How Genesyx collects and uses your information when you join the waitlist."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  type="page"
  summary="When you join the Genesyx waitlist we store your email address and the programme you chose, only so we can tell you when it is ready. We never sell your data, and you can ask us to delete it at any time."
  noindex
  updated={new Date("2026-09-30")}
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Genesyx Ltd (company number 16913651), Unit 8 Axiom, Orbital Park, Ashford TN24 0AA, United
    Kingdom, is the data controller for information collected on this website. You can contact us at
    <a href="mailto:info@genesyx.co.uk">info@genesyx.co.uk</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>When you join the waitlist we store:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your email address</li>
    <li>the programme you chose (XX or XY)</li>
    <li>
      the page you joined from, the website that referred you and any campaign tags in the link
    </li>
    <li>the date and time you joined, and a record that you agreed to receive launch emails</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not use advertising or analytics cookies on the waitlist form.</p>

  <h2>Why, and our legal basis</h2>
  <p>
    We use your details only to email you about the release of your chosen programme. Our legal
    basis is your consent, which you give when you join. We never sell your data or share it for
    marketing by anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
  <p>
    Your details are stored with our database provider, Supabase, on servers in the European
    Economic Area (Ireland).
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep your details until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete them.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to see, correct or delete your data, or withdraw your consent, at any time: every
    email we send includes an unsubscribe link, or write to
    <a href="mailto:info@genesyx.co.uk">info@genesyx.co.uk</a>. If you are unhappy with how we
    handle your data, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at
    <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk</a>.
  </p>
</GuideLayout>
